---
title: Figure 3.8 — Diagramme de séquence — Exécution, preuves et validation
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Prestataire
    actor Client
    participant FE as Web / Mobile
    participant API as Django REST
    participant Chat as ChatService
    participant Track as TrackingService
    participant Proof as ProofService
    participant AI as analysis_service
    participant WS as WebSocket
    participant Celery as Celery Beat
    participant ESC as EscrowService
    participant Notif as NotificationService
    participant MM as MetaMask
    participant SC as EscrowContract

    Note over Prestataire,SC: Exécution (souvent déjà in_progress après caution)

    Prestataire->>Chat: Messages mission
    Chat->>WS: broadcast
    WS-->>Client: chat live

    loop GPS
        Prestataire->>Track: position
        Track->>WS: gps_update
        WS-->>Client: carte live
    end

    Note over Prestataire,SC: Preuves

    Prestataire->>FE: Upload photo / signature / QR
    FE->>Proof: POST /api/proofs/
    Proof->>AI: flou, luminosité, EXIF, géo
    AI-->>Proof: indicateurs
    Prestataire->>FE: submit_proof
    FE->>API: POST .../submit_proof/
    API-->>FE: status=submitted
    API->>Notif: proofs_submitted
    API->>Celery: planifie auto-validation 48h

    opt Ancrage preuves
        FE->>MM: submitProof(missionId, proofHash)
        MM->>SC: tx
        FE->>API: record-proof
    end

    Note over Prestataire,SC: Validation

    alt Client valide
        Client->>FE: validate
        FE->>API: POST .../validate/
    else Timeout 48h
        Celery->>API: process_auto_validations
    end

    API->>ESC: release 95% / 5%
    API->>API: update reputation
    API-->>FE: status=completed
    Note over FE: Compte à rebours échéance arrêté

    opt Ancrage final
        FE->>MM: validateMission
        FE->>API: sync / record
    end

    FE-->>Client: Mission terminée
    FE-->>Prestataire: Fonds libérés
